{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1329842-origin-cults-in-non-obvious-communities","id":1329842,"title":"[Origin] Cults in non-obvious communities","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-08-08T00:46:50-07:00","id":1329842,"title":"[Origin] Cults in non-obvious communities","content":"I (very) slowly preparing my Origin game and I look for some inspirations. One of most needed for me are Cults, as I do not want to use direct Gods in my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1275725-2e-setting-hack-gods-in-hiding-and-new-mythic-age\">Gods in Hiding</a> hack game - and too sustain <i>Iron Myth</i> level, described in <b>Origin</b> book. ( <b>Origin</b>, p.135 )<br /> <br /> <i>'The World is not entirely the same as ours. Cults of Gods now ignored still have power, and the paths of their devotees can cross the lives of others to guide them on their way. It can mean repeated encounters with followers of a particular divinity, seeing images of their own face spray-painted on walls, or having dreams that raise their mortal concerns to the level of myth.'</i><br /> <br /> I just look for ideas <i>where</i> and <i>how</i> can Cults operate in modern society, hiding it's presence. Let's number ideas, it can make a nice list. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Here is mine:<br /> <br /> 1. <b>Aesir Cult in local mafia</b> - Many of Aesir Gods are war or warrior deities, making violence they favorite way of life. Adherents in local organised crime can more easily show their devotion and martial prowess, breaking the law they think are needless or harmful. <b>Typical Patrons: </b>Odin, Tyr, Vidar","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-08T01:16:32-07:00","id":1329847,"title":"","content":"The German craftsmen's associations, which grew out of medieval guilds, would be good candidates for this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/sunkencastles\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Sunken Castles, Evil Poodles</b></a> is creating Public Domain translations of German folklore!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://german-geek.blogspot.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><b>A German Geek</b></a> - my gaming blog!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10279-j\u00fcrgen-hubert","name":"J\u00fcrgen Hubert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-08T02:08:33-07:00","id":1329850,"title":"","content":"This is a pretty minor thing, but I don't think Tyr would condone a mafia lifestyle. Dude was a God of Oaths, and of Honor. Like, he lost his hand because he made an oath to Fenrir, which he broke. Really, if anybody were to back that lifestyle it'd be Odin and Thor.<br /> <br /> As for some Cults working in Semi-Secret ideas...<br /> <br /> 2. A cult of Hestia operates several power plants, claiming that as she is the Lady of the Hearth, Hestia clearly also counts power plants (which provide warmth and light to countless homes) as under her purview.<br /> <br /> 3. A Cult of Hades that shakes down mining companies, demanding tribute in exchange for how the miners infringe upon the domain of Hades and take the wealth that belongs to him.<br /> <br /> 4. Lugh Worshippers running several artifact smuggling rings, because Lugh never met a fancy foreign Relic he didn't want to steal. That's how he got the Luin for the Tuatha, after all!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-08T02:59:56-07:00","id":1329857,"title":"","content":"Consider all those weird fraternities and sororities, especially ones catering to the upper classes. Assume that at least half of them pay homage to some non-Christian deity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/sunkencastles\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Sunken Castles, Evil Poodles</b></a> is creating Public Domain translations of German folklore!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://german-geek.blogspot.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><b>A German Geek</b></a> - my gaming blog!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10279-j\u00fcrgen-hubert","name":"J\u00fcrgen Hubert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-08T03:59:13-07:00","id":1329865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>J\u00fcrgen Hubert</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1329842-origin-cults-in-non-obvious-communities?p=1329857#post1329857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Assume that at least half of them pay homage to some non-Christian deity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like the real ones...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-08T04:53:01-07:00","id":1329871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1329842-origin-cults-in-non-obvious-communities?p=1329850#post1329850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a pretty minor thing, but I don't think Tyr would condone a mafia lifestyle. Dude was a God of Oaths, and of Honor. Like, he lost his hand because he made an oath to Fenrir, which he broke. Really, if anybody were to back that lifestyle it'd be Odin and Thor.</div> </div> </div> </div>Real world Mafia ( Italian one ) is all about <a href=\"https://www.businessinsider.com/italian-police-heres-what-a-mafia-loyalty-oath-looks-like-2014-11?IR=T\" target=\"_blank\">Loyalty, Oaths and (specific interpreted ) Honor ( of mafia 'soldiers' )</a>. Tyr is not God of Law, only God of Oaths - as you pointed - so sustaining Mafia traditions is really in his area.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-08T07:28:55-07:00","id":1329885,"title":"","content":"So i don't imagine them as exactly hidden but i have thought of this cult.<br /> I have thought of a cult in The World that is mainly composed of History students where what they do is they catalog relics. Who has them, where they're from, are the relic an offshoot from a previous relic, etc.<br /> Now the cataloging is all in books and papers and they try to avoid actually interacting with scions (cause thats dangerous).<br /> But a small group dedicate themselves to bringing unowned relics back to the cultures that is their origin.<br /> Another group believes that they should be custodians of said relics and find worthy scions to give them back to.<br /> There is tension between the two groups.<br /> Still can't manage to think of a name that i like.<br /> The factiond abovenwould respectively be called The Reclaimers and The Custodians. And i imagine each would have derisive nicknames for the other.<br /> But i'm still unsure what to name the cult as a whole.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-08T08:26:43-07:00","id":1329895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1329842-origin-cults-in-non-obvious-communities?p=1329871#post1329871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Real world Mafia ( Italian one ) is all about <a href=\"https://www.businessinsider.com/italian-police-heres-what-a-mafia-loyalty-oath-looks-like-2014-11?IR=T\" target=\"_blank\">Loyalty, Oaths and (specific interpreted ) Honor ( of mafia 'soldiers' )</a>. Tyr is not God of Law, only God of Oaths - as you pointed - so sustaining Mafia traditions is really in his area.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that is using a very modern understanding of Oaths. Oaths and swearing are a fundamental part of the early Icelandic legal system, and then there is the huge issues the Norse have with crimes committed in secret (such as how if you kill someone publicly and state it, it is not murder but a killing, but if you kill someone privately and conceal it, it is murder) I don't think Tyr, or any of the Aesir, would be comfortable with the Mafia in the slightest. Sure, there might be oaths and loyalty, but the Norse are <i>very</i> invested in society and law and rules. Sure, if you strip Tyr of his social context he might work, but I don't think in his original cultural context the Aesir would be that comfortable with this sort of thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-08T10:25:57-07:00","id":1329920,"title":"","content":"So what would be a good cult to be at the centre of a mafia organization, then?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24028-mike-mccall","name":"Mike McCall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24028_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-08T11:41:23-07:00","id":1329942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mike McCall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1329842-origin-cults-in-non-obvious-communities?p=1329920#post1329920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what would be a good cult to be at the centre of a mafia organization, then?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe the Theoi, as typical as it may be? Like, big on family and all that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-08T12:09:47-07:00","id":1329950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1329842-origin-cults-in-non-obvious-communities?p=1329942#post1329942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe the Theoi, as typical as it may be? Like, big on family and all that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like your idea. The Theoi in Greek myths are pretty family business thing, \u201cWe fight each other, we hate each other, but we are the gods and no one mess with any us without messing with all of us\u201d. The Roman versions were more about community, legions and war, so using the roman names would not fit well,","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-08T14:35:10-07:00","id":1329974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1329842-origin-cults-in-non-obvious-communities?p=1329950#post1329950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like your idea. The Theoi in Greek myths are pretty family business thing, \u201cWe fight each other, we hate each other, but we are the gods and no one mess with any us without messing with all of us\u201d. The Roman versions were more about community, legions and war, so using the roman names would not fit well,</div> </div> </div> </div>In my 20s game, one of my players is a Chosen of Persephone, and she's the granddaughter of the local mafia boss. Persephone feels kinship with a fellow precious lady of the Underworld.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}